{"id":"mahabharata-4-013","work":"mahabharata","part":4,"partName":"विराटपर्व","partNameEn":"Virata Parva","unit":13,"title":"त्रयोदशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 13 · Kichaka desires Draupadi","summary":{"en":"In the tenth month of their stay, Kichaka, the powerful commander of Virata's army and brother of Queen Sudeshna, sees Draupadi and is overcome by desire. He woos her with promises of wealth, and she rejects him, warning that her Gandharva husbands will kill him.","kn":"ವಾಸದ ಹತ್ತನೆಯ ತಿಂಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ವಿರಾಟಸೇನೆಯ ಪ್ರಬಲ ಸೇನಾಪತಿ, ಸುದೇಷ್ಣೆಯ ಸಹೋದರ ಕೀಚಕನು ದ್ರೌಪದಿಯನ್ನು ಕಂಡು ಕಾಮಾಂಧನಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಸಂಪತ್ತಿನ ಭರವಸೆಯಿಂದ ಅವಳನ್ನು ಒಲಿಸಲು ಯತ್ನಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಗಂಧರ್ವ ಪತಿಗಳು ಕೊಲ್ಲುವರೆಂದು ಎಚ್ಚರಿಸಿ ಅವಳು ನಿರಾಕರಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ.","hi":"वहाँ रहने के दसवें महीने में विराट की सेना का शक्तिशाली सेनापति और रानी सुदेष्णा का भाई कीचक द्रौपदी को देखकर काम से विह्वल हो जाता है। वह धन के वचनों से उन्हें लुभाता है, और वे उसे ठुकराते हुए चेतावनी देती हैं कि उनके गन्धर्व पति उसे मार डालेंगे।","te":"నివాసపు పదవ నెలలో విరాటసేన బలమైన సేనాపతి, సుదేష్ణ సోదరుడు కీచకుడు ద్రౌపదిని చూసి కామవశుడవుతాడు. సంపద వాగ్దానాలతో ఆమెను లోబరచుకోవాలని ప్రయత్నిస్తాడు; గంధర్వ భర్తలు చంపుతారని హెచ్చరించి ఆమె నిరాకరిస్తుంది.","ta":"தங்கிய பத்தாம் மாதத்தில் விராடனின் படைத் தலைவனும் ஸுதேஷ்ணை அரசியின் சகோதரனுமான வலிய கீசகன் திரௌபதியைக் கண்டு காமவசப்படுகிறான். செல்வம் தருவதாக வாக்களித்து அவளை வசப்படுத்த முயல, கந்தர்வக் கணவர்கள் அவனைக் கொல்வார்கள் என்று எச்சரித்து அவள் மறுக்கிறாள்.","ml":"താമസം തുടങ്ങി പത്താം മാസത്തിൽ, വിരാടന്റെ സേനാനായകനും സുദേഷ്ണ രാജ്ഞിയുടെ സഹോദരനുമായ ശക്തനായ കീചകൻ ദ്രൗപദിയെ കാണുന്നു; അവൻ അവളിൽ മോഹം കൊണ്ട് മതിമറക്കുന്നു. ധനം വാഗ്ദാനം ചെയ്ത് അവൻ അവളെ വശീകരിക്കാൻ നോക്കുന്നു. അവൾ അവനെ നിരസിക്കുന്നു; തന്റെ ഗന്ധർവഭർത്താക്കന്മാർ അവനെ കൊല്ലുമെന്ന് മുന്നറിയിപ്പും നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 4.13; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Dec  1 2011","sections":[{"title":"कीचकवधपर्व","titleEn":"Kichakavadha Parva (Slaying of Kichaka)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"वसमानेषु पार्थेषु मत्स्यस्य नगरे तदा ।\nमहारथेषु छन्नेषु मासा दश समत्ययुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While the Parthas lived thus hidden, those great charioteers in the Matsya city, ten months passed."}},{"n":2,"text":"याज्ञसेनी सुदेष्णां तु शुश्रूषन्ती विशां पते ।\nअवसत्परिचारार्हा सुदुःखं जनमेजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yajnasena's daughter, serving Sudeshna, lived in great misery, though she deserved to be served herself, Janamejaya."}},{"n":3,"text":"तथा चरन्तीं पाञ्चालीं सुदेष्णाया निवेशने ।\nसेनापतिर्विराटस्य ददर्श जलजाननाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the Panchali went about in Sudeshna's house, Virata's commander-in-chief saw the lotus-faced woman."}},{"n":4,"text":"तां दृष्ट्वा देवगर्भाभां चरन्तीं देवतामिव ।\nकीचकः कामयामास कामबाणप्रपीडितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing her moving like a goddess, radiant as a child of the gods, Kichaka was struck by the arrows of desire and wanted her."}},{"n":5,"text":"स तु कामाग्निसंतप्तः सुदेष्णामभिगम्य वै ।\nप्रहसन्निव सेनानीरिदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Burning with the fire of passion, the commander went to Sudeshna and, smiling as it were, spoke these words."}},{"n":6,"text":"नेयं पुरा जातु मयेह दृष्टा\nराज्ञो विराटस्य निवेशने शुभा ।\nरूपेण चोन्मादयतीव मां भृशं\nगन्धेन जाता मदिरेव भामिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I have never seen this beautiful woman before in King Virata's house. By her beauty, and her fragrance like wine, this lady seems almost to drive me mad.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"का देवरूपा हृदयंगमा शुभे\nआचक्ष्व मे का च कुतश्च शोभना ।\nचित्तं हि निर्मथ्य करोति मां वशे\nन चान्यदत्रौषधमद्य मे मतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Who is this charming, godlike beauty? Tell me, who and from where is this lovely woman? She churns my mind and brings me under her power; I think no other medicine can help me now.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"अहो तवेयं परिचारिका शुभा\nप्रत्यग्ररूपा प्रतिभाति मामियम् ।\nअयुक्तरूपं हि करोति कर्म ते\nप्रशास्तु मां यच्च ममास्ति किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Ah, this lovely servant of yours seems to me fresh and new; she does work unfit for her. Let her rule me and all that I have.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"प्रभूतनागाश्वरथं महाधनं\nसमृद्धियुक्तं बहुपानभोजनम् ।\nमनोहरं काञ्चनचित्रभूषणं\nगृहं महच्छोभयतामियं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let her adorn my large house, with its many elephants, horses and chariots, great wealth, plenty of drink and food, delightful and decorated with gold.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"ततः सुदेष्णामनुमन्त्र्य कीचक-\nस्ततः समभ्येत्य नराधिपात्मजाम् ।\nउवाच कृष्णामभिसान्त्वयंस्तदा\nमृगेन्द्रकन्यामिव जम्बुको वने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Kichaka, having consulted Sudeshna, came to the king's daughter-like maid and spoke soothingly to Krishna, like a jackal to a lion's cub in the forest."}},{"n":11,"text":"इदं च रूपं प्रथमं च ते वयो\nनिरर्थकं केवलमद्य भामिनि ।\nअधार्यमाणा स्रगिवोत्तमा यथा\nन शोभसे सुन्दरि शोभना सती ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This beauty and your first youth, lady, are wasted now; like a fine garland not worn, you do not shine, lovely one, though you are good and beautiful.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"त्यजामि दारान्मम ये पुरातना\nभवन्तु दास्यस्तव चारुहासिनि ।\nअहं च ते सुन्दरि दासवत्स्थितः\nसदा भविष्ये वशगो वरानने ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I shall give up my old wives; let them be your servants, sweet-smiling lady. And I myself shall stay at your command like a slave, fair-faced one, always in your power.\""}},{"text":"द्रौपद्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Draupadi said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"अप्रार्थनीयामिह मां सूतपुत्राभिमन्यसे ।\nविहीनवर्णां सैरन्ध्रीं बीभत्सां केशकारिकाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son of a charioteer, you think of one who is not to be desired, a sairandhri of poor appearance, an ugly hairdresser."}},{"n":14,"text":"परदारास्मि भद्रं ते न युक्तं त्वयि सांप्रतम् ।\nदयिताः प्राणिनां दारा धर्मं समनुचिन्तय ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am another man's wife; may you be well, but this is not proper for you. Wives are dear to living beings; think on dharma."}},{"n":15,"text":"परदारे न ते बुद्धिर्जातु कार्या कथंचन ।\nविवर्जनं ह्यकार्याणामेतत्सत्पुरुषव्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Never turn your mind to another's wife in any way; avoiding forbidden acts is the vow of good men."}},{"n":16,"text":"मिथ्याभिगृध्नो हि नरः पापात्मा मोहमास्थितः ।\nअयशः प्राप्नुयाद्घोरं सुमहत्प्राप्नुयाद्भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who falsely covets and is evil-minded, caught in delusion, will gain terrible disgrace and very great danger."}},{"n":17,"text":"मा सूतपुत्र हृष्यस्व माद्य त्यक्ष्यसि जीवितम् ।\nदुर्लभामभिमन्वानो मां वीरैरभिरक्षिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do not rejoice, son of a charioteer; do not give up your life today by desiring me, hard to win and guarded by heroes."}},{"n":18,"text":"न चाप्यहं त्वया शक्या गन्धर्वाः पतयो मम ।\nते त्वां निहन्युः कुपिताः साध्वलं मा व्यनीनशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You cannot have me; my husbands are gandharvas. In their anger they would kill you; stop, do not destroy yourself."}},{"n":19,"text":"अशक्यरूपैः पुरुषैरध्वानं गन्तुमिच्छसि ।\nयथा निश्चेतनो बालः कूलस्थः कूलमुत्तरम् ।\nतर्तुमिच्छति मन्दात्मा तथा त्वं कर्तुमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"You want to walk a road that men of weak resolve cannot walk, like a foolish child standing on one bank who wants to cross to the far bank."}},{"n":20,"text":"अन्तर्महीं वा यदि वोर्ध्वमुत्पतेः\nसमुद्रपारं यदि वा प्रधावसि ।\nतथापि तेषां न विमोक्षमर्हसि\nप्रमाथिनो देवसुता हि मे वराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whether you go into the depths of the earth, or leap into the sky, or run across the ocean, you will not escape them, for my noble husbands, sons of gods, are destroyers."}},{"n":21,"text":"त्वं कालरात्रीमिव कश्चिदातुरः\nकिं मां दृढं प्रार्थयसेऽद्य कीचक ।\nकिं मातुरङ्के शयितो यथा शिशु-\nश्चन्द्रं जिघृक्षुरिव मन्यसे हि माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kichaka, why do you so fiercely desire me today, like a sick man who longs for the night of death? Are you like a baby lying on his mother's lap, who wants to seize the moon?"}}]}]}